# The Windows disk inside this computer is not offered in the file
# manager. Opening it (udisks' filesystem-mount-system) used to be
# granted to her account without a password, so any program running as
# her could mount Windows read-write -- and writing to a Windows that
# is hibernated (Fast Startup) loses what it had open. Her files come
# across from it read-only (Ferry, as root); nothing else touches it.
# Hidden rather than refused, so the file manager shows no button that
# only answers "not authorised". A USB disk is still hers to open.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{ID_BUS}!="usb", ENV{ID_FS_TYPE}=="ntfs|BitLocker", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
